config DRM_M9X
	tristate "Matrox M9/Phoenix clean-room driver"
	depends on DRM && PCI
	select DRM_CLIENT_SELECTION
	select DRM_EXEC
	select DRM_GEM_DMA_HELPER
	select I2C
	select I2C_ALGOBIT
	select DRM_GEM_VRAM_HELPER
	help
	  Independent clean-room bring-up driver for Matrox M9/Phoenix device
	  102b:0540.  It has no dependency on the Parhelia P-series module.

	  m9_enable=1 is required before the driver binds.  It exposes DMA32 GEM
	  and a validate-only command interface.  m9_render_diag=1 is additionally
	  required for the kernel-owned writeback-fence diagnostic.  Guarded warm
	  KMS requires m9_kms=1 and the separately gated direct scanout path
	  requires m9_kms_scanout=1.  m9_triangle_diag=1 permits allocation and
	  synchronous execution of the kernel-owned, vendor-framed first-triangle
	  diagnostic after its cold transitions and sequence-zero setup retire.

	  If compiled as a module, it will be called m9x_drm.
